  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nWe aim to improve upon the current best bound by using a hierarchical optimization strategy. The key bottlenecks in the previous approach were:\n- Local optima due to insufficient exploration\n- Slow convergence from basic initializations\n- Single fixed resolution\n\nOur approach combines:\n- Multi-scale optimization (128\u2192256\u2192512)\n- Intelligent selection from multiple initial conditions\n- Gradient descent with auto-adjusted learning rates\n- Fitness-based selection algorithm for initial guesses\n- Early termination when close to target\n\nThe central idea is to interleave targeted optimization with coarse-to-fine resolution that maintains diversity while ensuring sufficient search time. This reduces the risk of getting stuck in local optima while staying within the 1100s budget.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\nWe optimize over n-point samples with:\n- h \u2208 [0,1]^n\n- \u2211h_i = n/2\n- Objective: min max_k \u2211_{i=0}^{n-|k|} h[i] * (1 - h[i+k])\n- Resolution: 128, 256, 512 points\n- Dimensions mappings: keep n=2048 max\n- Validity check: \u2211h_i = n/2 and 0\u2264h_i\u22641\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1100):\n  rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n  start = time.time()\n  time_left = lambda: budget_s - (time.time()-start)\n\n  # Candidate management\n  def make_candidates(n, rng, diversity=5, balance=0.5):\n    candidates = []\n    # Scaled Thue-Morse as base\n    tm = thue_morse(n)\n    for _ in range(diversity):\n      h = thue_morse(n)\n      h = project_onto_box_sum(h, n/2)\n      # Random perturbation\n      if balance is not None:\n        h[0]=balance\n      candidates.append(h+np.random.normal(0.01, scale=0.05, size=n))\n    return candidates\n\n  # Multi-scale optimization sequence\n  scales = [128, 256, 512]\n  best_candidate = None\n  best_score = float('inf')\n\n  for scale in scales:\n    n_points = scale\n    if best_candidate is not None and best_candidate.shape[0] == n_points:\n      # Reuse previous best\n      best_score = compute_c5(best_candidate)\n      continue\n      \n    # Fitness-based sampling\n    fitnesses = []\n    if time_left() < 5:\n      break\n      \n    trial_candidates = []\n    T0 = time_left() / (len(scales) * scale ** 1.5 / 80)\n    if T0 > 0:\n      base_candidates = make_candidates(min(8, int(1+(scale/64)**0.5)), rng)\n      for cand_base in base_candidates:\n        cand = cand_base.copy()\n        cand = slsqp_optimize_candidate(cand, budget_s=10)\n        score = compute_c5(cand)\n        fitnesses.append((score, cand))\n        trial_candidates.append(cand)\n        \n    if not fitnesses:\n      cand = base_candidates[0]\n      score = compute_c5(cand)\n      fitnesses.append((score, cand))\n      trial_candidates.append(cand)\n      \n    fitnesses.sort()  # Best first\n    best_known = None\n    best_score_known = float('inf')\n\n    # Optimization with adaptive gradient descent\n    for i, (score, cand) in enumerate(fitnesses):\n      if time_left() < 5: exit('Timed out')\n      \n      # Auto-configure learning rate based score\n      eta = 0.1 * (0.95 ** (10000-score*100))\n      beta = 0.9 + 0.1 * (score-0.38)\n\n      # Perform gradient descent\n      cand_gd = gradient_descent_momentum_custom(\n        cand.copy(), n_iter=min(20000, int(time_left()*10)), \n        step0=0.2, beta=beta, rng=rng, time_left=time_left\n      )\n      score_gd = compute_c5(cand_gd)\n      \n      if score_gd < best_score_known:\n        best_known = cand_gd\n        best_score_known = score_gd\n        \n      if score_gd < best_score:\n        best_score = score_gd\n        best_candidate = cand_gd.copy()\n        if best_score <= 0.3808:\n          break  # Early win\n\n    if best_known is not None:\n      print(f\"At scale {scale}: score {best_known}\")\n      if best_known is not None and best_score is None or compute_c5(best_known) < best_score:\n        best_score = compute_c5(best_known)\n        best_candidate = best_known.copy()\n        \n  return(best_candidate or thue_morse(scales[-1]), best_score, scales[-1])\n\n4. Search choices:\n- Upper confidence bound for initial selection\n- Adaptive learning rate decay (\u03b7)\n- Momentum parameter \u03b2 adjusted based on per-scale performance\n- Early termination when below 0.3808\n\n5. Robustness design:\n- When projection fails: fallback to annealed optimization\n- When gradient descent diverges: clip updates to [-0.1, 0.1]\n- Missing initial estimates: use generic random initialization\n- Time constraints: gracefully fall back to last known candidate\n\n6. Runtime safety:\n- score = compute_c5(h) at candidate verification\n- time_left() monitor at every major operation\n- Automatic scaling with resolution\n- Feasibility checked by compute_c5()\n- Budget capping: max_iter proportional to available time",
